// Generated by scripts/build-civilian-ships.py. Verbatim; do not edit by hand.
const SCN_CIVILIAN={ships:[{"name": "Hyperyacht Somniferum", "cost": 80, "tonnage": "L", "art": "hyperyacht_somniferum.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "9\"", "scan": "6\"", "sig": "4\"", "hull": 6, "es": "4+", "ks": "5+", "bs": "6+", "g": "1", "special": "Unique"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Party Poppers", "arc": "F/S", "attack": "3", "lock": "4+", "damage": "1", "type": "E", "special": "Status"}], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Unique", "text": "You may only take one Group of this Ship."}], "famousPrefix": "Only ship of the class:", "famous": ["Hyperyacht Somniferum"], "lore": ["The Hyperyacht Somniferum is not a sight civilized governments want to see on situation reports. Colloquially known as \"the party bus\", a spike in crime and illegal substances usually follows in its wake. Somniferum's current owner is the \"Master of Ceremonies\" Maeby Hy. The Somniferum is almost unrecognisable from its initial configuration as an Eden Aerospace Systems Luxury Liner. Lab explosions, combat damage, and ad-hoc refits have all added to it's hodge-podge appearance.", "One of these many changes to the ship is the addition of a peculiar weapon system. While it has no official name, the crew and any who face it have dubbed it \"Party Poppers\". This weapon system fires armour piercing fragmenting flechettes that disperse airborne narcotics and electromagnetic interference into its target. Far too small and numerous to effectively track, this weapon is able to bypass the majority of a ship's point defences and deliver strikes straight to the hull.", "The Somniferum is rarely seen over combat zones, preferring to stick to those planets that are safe enough for civilian travel. While able to defend itself against small time competitors, the ship isn't built for combat. More often than not, the Somniferum will make a hasty exit from a planet as soon as it detects any law enforcement on an intercept course."]}, {"name": "L-Type Barge", "cost": null, "tonnage": "L", "art": "l_type_barge.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "10”", "scan": "4”", "sig": "3”", "hull": 4, "es": "3+", "ks": "6+", "bs": "5+", "g": "1", "special": "Descent, Boardable, Civilian Transport"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Asteroid Clearance Laser", "arc": "F/S/R", "attack": "2", "lock": "4+", "damage": "1", "type": "E", "special": "Close Action"}], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Descent", "text": ""}, {"name": "Boardable", "text": ""}, {"name": "Civilian Transport", "text": ""}], "famousPrefix": "Known ships of the class:", "famous": ["Scum Runner", "Box ‘n’ Go", "Haulie", "LK-5 (Kalium)", "Oxy-Box (Vega Scrapfleet)"], "lore": ["The L-Type Barge was one of the most ubiquitous civilian bulk transports seen during early expansion into the cradle worlds. While relatively cheap and easy to produce, its Foldspace and sublight drives were poor at the time and were quickly superceeded by those installed on newer ships, like the Seneca Hauler. Despite its obsolete hardware the L-Type is much more durable than other ships its age. Featuring more internal bracing than neccesary, it could simply weather any attempts to stop it from delivering its cargo.", "It’s this durability that saw many survive the Battle of Vega, though not all unscathed. While tough, this ship’s foldspace drive takes an ungainly amount of time to fully spin up, this saw many stranded over Vega while their fellow abandonists followed their enigmatic saviour. Now many of these form support ships in the Vega Scrapfleet, being retrofitted with surplus colonisation equipment, making full use of their cargo space.", "Kalium still operates near pristine versions of these ships, suggesting that they still produce these in numbers. The Office of Naval Intelligence has identified no less than 6 unique L-Type Barges operating in the Kalium Navy, all operating within expected parameters of a ship their type. While new, Kalium has clearly neglected to bring these ships design specs up to even its long standing contemporaries."]}, {"name": "LKS Dredger", "cost": 65, "tonnage": "L", "art": "lks_dredger.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "8\"", "scan": "6\"", "sig": "6\"", "hull": 6, "es": "4+", "ks": "5+", "bs": "6+", "g": "1-2", "special": "Vectored, Industrial Design"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Mining Laser", "arc": "F", "attack": "3", "lock": "2+", "damage": "2", "type": "E", "special": "Burnthrough-2, Close Action"}], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Industrial Design", "text": "Improve this Group’s Backup save by 2 when rolling to save hits due to Debris Fields."}], "famousPrefix": "Noted ships of the class:", "famous": ["Dredger", "Silt Siphon", "Ground Town"], "lore": ["A relentless machine of industry, built to mulch, sift, and extract until its timer runs dry. It drills deep, rips apart rock, and spits out raw profit, indifferent to the hands that keep it running. No legacy, no ownership, just a contract ticking toward expiration. When time is up, it moves on, leaving its crew behind, waiting for the next company to stake its claim on the battered frame. Inside, the workers endure the constant grind, wedged between failing systems and the unyielding demand for productivity. Comfort is non-existent, maintenance is endless.", "Equipped with a heavy duty drill and front mounted mining array, this vessel doesn't just extract minerals, it carves deep trenches into asteroid surfaces and space debris, kicking up clouds of pulverized rock and metallic sediment. A network of sediment filters and gravity sifting tanks separates valuable ore from dust before storing the processed materials in its cargo bays.", "Prominently displayed on the ship's exterior, the countdown display isn't a warning, it's a fact. The contract will expire, and if it doesn't get topped up, the vessel moves on to whatever comes next. Passed from one mining company to the next, these hand me down workhorses run until their rental contracts dry up. Refurbished just enough to stay functional, they degrade with every transfer, patched, battered, barely space worthy, considered scrap with engines.", "Upper management doesn't care about the ship, only the ore it pulls in before time runs out. The crew works under relentless pressure, knowing there's no guarantee of renewal.", "When the timer hits zero, it's out of their hands. Either the contract gets extended, or the ship moves on.", "Despite its size, the colossal vessel remains a world of tight corridors for its 190 crew members. Dust and grime clings to every surface, settling in forgotten corners and coating equipment in a fine greasy layer. Minimal comforts, constant maintenance, and the daily expectation that something will break."]}, {"name": "MK Mass Transporter", "cost": 41, "tonnage": "L", "art": "mk_mass_transporter.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "10\"", "scan": "4\"", "sig": "4\"", "hull": 5, "es": "5+", "ks": "6+", "bs": "N/A", "g": "1-2", "special": "Descent, Rare"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Deterrence Missiles", "arc": "F/S", "attack": "4", "lock": "3+", "damage": "1", "type": "K", "special": "Close Action"}], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Descent", "text": "When attacking a City or a Descent Ship in Atmosphere, that attack always hits on a 6+ and can never cause a critical.\nWhen attacking a non-Descent Ship in Atmosphere, reduce the lock of Weapons attacking it by 1.\nWhen attacking into Orbit from Atmosphere, any attack always hits on a 6+.\nA non-Descent Ship that ends its activation in Atmosphere takes D3 damage. Colossal Ships take 2D3 damage instead."}, {"name": "Rare", "text": "You may only take one Group of this Ship in a Skirmish-sized game, two in a Clash, three in a Battle, and four in a Reconquest."}, {"name": "Mercenary", "text": "This Ship may be used in any Fleet regardless of faction. When taken as part of your fleet, this Ship loses its Boardable rule."}, {"name": "Bulk Lighter", "text": "While a Ship with this rule is on the table, you have access to the following Ability:\n\nBattalion Support (1AP): Once per activation, when you deploy Battalions from a Group on any Orbital Layer within 6” of a friendly Ship with the Bulk Lighter rule, choose one of the launching Asset types. If the chosen Asset is either Dropships or Drop Pods, place an additional Battalion. If the chosen Asset is Bulk Landers, place an additional two Battalions. Other Launch Assets are unaffected by this Ability."}], "famousPrefix": "", "famous": [], "lore": ["It’s a tough, thankless job hauling cargo from ground to space, but the Maganum Kinematics Mass Transporter takes it all in its stride. This reliable workhorse can be frequently seen flitting between orbit and atmosphere collecting and dispensing valuable cargo. During the reconquest, the durable, yet lightly armoured spaceframe of this vessel was used as a second line support vessel assisting troopships in setting up forward operating bases. Full of prefabricated barricades, fire-support bunkers, and even command centres, this small hauler vastly improves the efficiency of troops deployed to combat zones. Keeping the war machine well equipped, well stocked, and with a relatively comfortable, if cramped base to strike out at Scourge targets from.", "Even though their primary contracts are with the UCM, Maganum Kinematics have sold many of these to other non government organisations. Various shipping magnates operate at least one of these reliable ships at each of their destinations. More surprisingly, even other factions have been making use of these vessels. The PHR stationed at Earth have requisitioned a pair of these ships, as well as Kalium counting no fewer than four of these vessels amongst its fleet, though only two have been seen operating in the vicinity of Earth."]}, {"name": "M.A.B. 67 Fuel Transport", "cost": 55, "tonnage": "L", "art": "mab_67_fuel_transport.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "9\"", "scan": "6\"", "sig": "4\"", "hull": 6, "es": "4+", "ks": "4+", "bs": "6+", "g": "1-2", "special": "Vectored"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Deterrence Missiles", "arc": "F/S", "attack": "4", "lock": "3+", "damage": "1", "type": "K", "special": "Alt-1, Close Action"}, {"name": "Ignite Reserves", "arc": "F/S/R", "attack": "0", "lock": "2+", "damage": "2", "type": "E", "special": "Alt-1, Close Action, Fusillade-2"}], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Vectored", "text": "This Ship may make an additional turn at any point during its movement, regardless of the Order its Group has taken."}, {"name": "Fuel Transporter", "text": "While a Ship with this rule is on the table, you have access to the following Ability:\n\nFully Fuelled (2AP): At the start of a friendly Group’s activation, if that Group is within 3” and on the same Orbital Layer as a Ship with the Fuel Transporter rule, the friendly Group increases its total movement (after Orders) by 3” this round. If that Group is on the Max Thrust order, it increases its total movement (after Orders) by 6” this round instead.\nIf the friendly Group is C Tonnage, that Group must be within 3” and on the same Orbital Layer as two Ships with the Fuel Transporter rule instead.\nShips with the Fuel Transporter rule are unaffected by this Ability."}, {"name": "Ignite Reserves", "text": "After completing an attack with this Weapon, this Ship is destroyed (a weapon with 0 Attack value does not roll to hit, does not cause any saves to be made, and does not inflict damage due to hits).\n\nWhen this Ship is destroyed (for any reason), it explodes with a Fuel Detonation effect and a range of 3”. Ships damaged by this explosion also gain a Fire token."}, {"name": "Mercenary", "text": "This Ship may be used in any Fleet regardless of faction. When taken as part of your fleet, this Ship loses its Boardable and Civilian Transport rules."}], "famousPrefix": "Famous ships of the class:", "famous": ["Fire in a Can", "Petrol Pusher (UCM)", "Jugnaut", "Juice Sluice", "Bottle Bearer (Vega Scrapfleet)", "Logistics Vessel KLV-822 (Kalium)"], "lore": ["The Maganum Asset Bureau was once one of the largest civilian infrastructure manufacturers in the colonies prior to the inception of the UCM. Hailing from a relatively quiet colony with a focus on agriculture, the M.A.B. developed and put into service a multitude of logistical vessels. Many were designed to transport Maganum’s bountiful harvests to other colony worlds, such as the M.A.B. 45 and 46, with holds designed to keep live seafood and store masses of frozen produce, keeping the colonies main source of protein moving.", "Then there was the M.A.B. 67, arguably, the Bureau’s most successful design. This transport is able to safely carry an exceptional volume of various types of fuel, from Maganum’s simple biofuels, to the hypercompressed metallic hydrogen that keeps the UCM war machine running. Built to exacting standards, the 67 has one of the strongest and most reliable power plants for a ship of its size. As it was never expected to see actual combat, the reactors do not have the automatic shutdown safeties of UCM combat ships, indeed if the ship were to see combat, it is quite possible that any damage to the reactors could cause a major containment breach, flooding compartments with highly volatile plasma.", "The ubiquity of the line meant that they were scattered far and wide at the time of the Scourge invasion, now there are 67’s amongst almost all the major players of the time. The UCM have continued to produce small numbers of this ship, while M.A.B. has dwindled, they still produce original and updated designs and have mostly superseded the 67 with the much more efficient 192, a built for purpose, clearly UCM design. The Scourge have re-purposed many of these ships into water transports and rarely use them for transporting fuel, while the PHR still make use of refit variants for their logistics purposes. Many of these have been seen in resistance hands, several are part of the Vega Scrapfleet and Kalium have seemingly gotten or reverse engineered the designs to produce more ships of the class, though are much more reckless with them than any other faction."]}, {"name": "Nirvana", "cost": null, "tonnage": "L", "art": "nirvana.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "9”", "scan": "4”", "sig": "3”", "hull": 6, "es": "4+", "ks": "6+", "bs": "-", "g": "1", "special": "Blooming, Boardable, Civilian Transport"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Asteroid Clearance Laser", "arc": "F/S/R", "attack": "2", "lock": "4+", "damage": "1", "type": "E", "special": "Close Action"}], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Blooming", "text": ""}, {"name": "Boardable", "text": ""}, {"name": "Civilian Transport", "text": ""}], "famousPrefix": "Known ships of the class:", "famous": ["Earth", "Eden Prime", "Asgard (destroyed)", "Elysium (Kalium)"], "lore": ["The Nirvana Class was designed as a mobile tourism hotspot. Each of the Cradle Worlds was represented in one ship of the class, with each rotating between systems to bring the sights of distant colonies close. Since the Scourge invasion, only four of these ships are accounted for. Earth and Eden Prime are currently in orbit around Aurum. Their serene presence is a reminder of the battle the UCM fight and are some of the most guarded civilian ships in orbit. The Asgard lies in ruins over Vega, an unfortunate victim of the first volley. A vent cannon tore through its vulnerable dome, incinerating all within. No one knows the exact number as the exact crew compliment was not recorded, but it was suspected over 1000 souls lost their lives in that instant.", "Somehow, the Elysium resides above Kalium. No one is sure how exactly it found its way there, but it is suspected that it was simply circumstance. A chance jump to a random foldspace node prior to the formation of the UCM. It is unknown how many of the remaining Cradle World Nirvana’s remain, as they have either fled with the abandonists at Vega, been destroyed beyond recognition, or usurped and absconded with by the Scourge for their own nefarious purposes.", "The mystery of one of the remaining Nirvana’s may soon be solved, as recent reconnaissance by the Lysander class UCMF Shadow’s Edge has spotted what appears to be an inactive hull that matches the appearance of an unknown Nirvana class. The Shadow’s edge was unable to investigate further, however, as multiple unknown signatures were detected in system."]}, {"name": "Precedent One", "cost": null, "tonnage": "L", "art": "precedent_one.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "9”", "scan": "4”", "sig": "3”", "hull": 6, "es": "4+", "ks": "6+", "bs": "-", "g": "1", "special": "Blooming, Boardable, Civilian Transport, Elite Fighter Escort"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Deterrence Missiles", "arc": "F/S", "attack": "4", "lock": "3+", "damage": "1", "type": "K", "special": "Close Action"}], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Blooming", "text": ""}, {"name": "Boardable", "text": ""}, {"name": "Civilian Transport", "text": ""}, {"name": "Elite Fighter Escort", "text": ""}], "famousPrefix": "Known ships of the class:", "famous": ["Precedent One", "Diplomacy One"], "lore": ["During the Reconquest, fleetyards throughout the Colonies were hard at work constructing a multitude of civilian and logistical ships. While retrofits to the ageing Princess Liner had kept them operational for far longer than intended, their age was starting to catch up with them. The Precedent One was more of a propaganda project than anything else, a ship designed to ferry dignitaries to recaptured Cradle Worlds for diplomatic talks but only under a minimal amount of danger.", "Only three ships of the class have been completed, one of which is a designated transport of UCM High Council members. Another is tasked with transporting diplomats to the Cradle Worlds friendly to the UCM, while the third is held in a secure location, should a replacement or decoy be required for either of the two in service."]}, {"name": "SLM-9 Resupply Hauler", "cost": 35, "tonnage": "L", "art": "slm_9_resupply_hauler.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "9\"", "scan": "4\"", "sig": "2\"", "hull": 5, "es": "3+", "ks": "5+", "bs": "6+", "g": "1", "special": "Vectored"}, "weapons": [], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Vectored", "text": "This Ship may make an additional turn at any point during its movement, regardless of the Order its Group has taken."}, {"name": "Resupply and Rearm", "text": "If this ship ends its movement in base contact with a friendly ship of Medium Tonnage or higher or a Space Station, pick one of the following:\nResupply: That Ship or Space Station recovers 3 Hull points and remove any Crippling Effect tokens.\nRearm: Increase the Limited-X value of any of that Ship or Space Station's Weapons and Launch Assets by 1 until the end of the round."}, {"name": "Flawed Design", "text": "This Ship cannot use its Resupply and Rearm rule if it is below half of its starting Hull."}, {"name": "Mercenary", "text": "This Ship may be used in any Fleet regardless of faction. When taken as part of your fleet, this Ship loses its Boardable rule."}], "famousPrefix": "Noted ships of the class:", "famous": ["Crate Expectations", "Right on Time", "Reliable"], "lore": ["A relic from the now liquidated Eden Void Logistics inc, the SLM-9 is a battle tested bulk logistics vessel, trusted for fleet replenishment in high risk environments. Though the company behind its design has since shuttered, the SLM-9 endures as a testament to their engineering prowess and affordability. Its metal cargo frame, hydraulic deployment arms and universal clamps ensure rapid, adaptable resupply of ordnance, fuel, and supplies anywhere. Rugged and inexpensive, the SLM-9 remains a reasonable choice for fleets needing a dependable workhorse at a fraction of the cost of newer models.", "Unlike conventional Logistics Vessels that unload cargo gradually, the SLM-9 releases its entire payload in a single, controlled operation. Hydraulic deployment arms manoeuvre the entire cargo bed outward, allowing for structured and efficient transfer without manual unloading.", "Built for adaptability, the SLM-9's pincer like grappling arms latch onto ships regardless of docking compatibility. Variable force actuators fine tune pressure, securing a stable hold without compromising hull integrity. Whether resupplying warships or assisting stranded vessels, its clamps ensure critical cargo transfer under any conditions.", "The SLM-9's hydraulic deployment arms are its defining feature, but also its greatest liability. If compromised by enemy fire or mechanical failure, the vessel loses its ability to unload cargo entirely, rendering it useless. A damaged deployment system means supplies remain trapped onboard, preventing fleet resupply and turning the ship into dead weight. While reinforced plating offers some protection, direct hits can buckle the arms, leading to catastrophic failure.", "Due to its critical vulnerability, the SLM-9 has begun to be phased out in favour of newer resupply haulers with reinforced unloading mechanisms and modular backup systems. The remaining SLM-9 units are considered outdated relics, still operational but increasingly rare."]}, {"name": "T-Type Tugboat", "cost": 60, "tonnage": "L", "art": "t_type_tugboat.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "6\"", "scan": "4\"", "sig": "3\"", "hull": 5, "es": "5+", "ks": "5+", "bs": "6+", "g": "1-4", "special": "Descent, Monitor, Vectored, Tugging Along"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Deterrence Missiles", "arc": "F/S", "attack": "4", "lock": "3+", "damage": "1", "type": "K", "special": "Close Action"}, {"name": "Drag to Hell", "arc": "F", "attack": "3", "lock": "3+", "damage": "2", "type": "C", "special": "Close Action"}], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Descent", "text": "When attacking a City or a Descent Ship in Atmosphere, that attack always hits on a 6+ and can never cause a critical.\nWhen attacking a non-Descent Ship in Atmosphere, reduce the lock of Weapons attacking it by 1.\nWhen attacking into Orbit from Atmosphere, any attack always hits on a 6+.\nA non-Descent Ship that ends its activation in Atmosphere takes D3 damage. Colossal Ships take 2D3 damage instead."}, {"name": "Monitor", "text": "Ships with this rule may not use Course Change or Max Thrust orders."}, {"name": "Vectored", "text": "This Ship may make an additional turn at any point during its movement, regardless of the Order its Group has taken."}, {"name": "Tugging Along", "text": "If this Ship is on General Quarters and in base contact with another Ship (friendly or enemy) you may have it Tug that Ship instead of moving normally. If you do, this Ship may turn as normal but only moves up to 3”. The other Ship is then moved the same distance in the same direction, retaining its original facing. Ships can only be tugged this way up to a maximum of 6” each round."}], "famousPrefix": "Known ships of the class:", "famous": ["Tug & Go", "Ride to Die", "Tugging Along", "T-104", "T-666 [destroyed]"], "lore": ["The T-Type was once a common sight across many shipyards. Due to the size of many pre-war ships, a way of moving these gargantuan vessels out of drydock was needed. T-Types were devised to be the answer to this sizeable problem. The first batch of these floated out of the assembly lines prior to the first Pathfinder, ready and waiting to guide it to a safe launching point. Since then, countless multitudes of these ships have been constructed. Most serve their entire service life in the void, however some are refitted as lunar landers once their superstructure becomes unusable for its intended purpose.", "Only a small amount of these were refit with foldspace drives, the majority were only designed to work around a single planet and its satellites. Those that were refit tend to be found in independent fleets, where they assist in swapping components on their larger vessels. T-Types are not built for any form of combat, though their internal bracing gives them a certain resilience, they are unable to weather any attack from dedicated combat ships.", "Some T-Types have been converted to function similarly to mines, albeit with a much more personal weapon system. These have weaponised their towing ability, captains with a death wish will attach their tug to an enemy vessel and set their engines to full. When performed right, this can violently tear vessels in half, though at the cost of the tugboat and its crew."]}, {"name": "EX-7 Packet Runner", "cost": 57, "tonnage": "L", "art": "ex7_packet_runner.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "6\"", "scan": "4\"", "sig": "3\"", "hull": 6, "es": "4+", "ks": "5+", "bs": "6+", "g": "1", "special": "Monitor, Reinforced Armour"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Deterrence Missiles", "arc": "F/S", "attack": "4", "lock": "3+", "damage": "1", "type": "K", "special": "Close Action"}], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Monitor", "text": "Ships with this rule may not use Course Change or Max Thrust orders."}, {"name": "Reinforced Armour", "text": "Weapons rolling to hit this Ship or its Group can only score criticals against it on a result of a 3 higher than its Lock value."}, {"name": "Feature Carrier", "text": "This ship starts the game carrying a single deployable Hangar Feature (see 7.4.2 Deploying Features and 11.3 Features)."}, {"name": "Space Trucker", "text": "This Ship's Hangar Deployable Feature can only be deployed to Space Stations (of any type)."}, {"name": "Mercenary", "text": "This Ship may be used in any Fleet regardless of faction. When taken as part of your fleet, this Ship loses its Boardable and Civilian Transport rules."}], "famousPrefix": "Known ships of the class:", "famous": ["Cargoer", "Pack Rat", "Porch Pirate (independents)", "Logistics Vessel KLV-302 (Kalium)"], "lore": ["The EX-7 Packet-Runner is a common courier craft used throughout the territories of the United Colonies of Mankind. Designed for routine parcel and sensitive package transport, it prioritizes simple construction and dependable operation over appearance or refinement. Most examples in service are visibly beaten up and poorly maintained, their worn hulls reflecting constant use and minimal upkeep.", "They are Built around a straightforward modular frame, similar to other workhorse craft like the T-Type utility haulers and the smaller VX-22 Flesners. The EX-7 typically consists of little more than the essentials: cockpit, drive assembly, and standardized cargo racks bolted into a compact hull with the cargo containers mounted underneath.", "Though rarely the focus of attention, EX-7 Packet-Runners move a constant flow of everyday freight between stations, depots, and outposts, quietly handling the unglamorous but essential task of keeping day-to-day logistics running. Colonial authorities have repurposed many of these ships for the express purpose of resupplying fighter and bomber support craft. Their cargo containers filled with factory-fresh compliments of fighters and bombers waiting for an appropriate launch platform. Experimental versions of these containers have been developed to effortlessly convert standardised hardpoints on space stations into makeshift hangar bays."]}, {"name": "Affluence Liner", "cost": null, "tonnage": "M", "art": "affluence_liner.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "14”", "scan": "6”", "sig": "3”", "hull": 12, "es": "4+", "ks": "5+", "bs": "-", "g": "1", "special": "Descent, Cloak-1, Boardable, Civilian Transport, Elite Fighter Escort, Unique"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Deterrence Missiles", "arc": "F/S", "attack": "4", "lock": "3+", "damage": "1", "type": "K", "special": "Close Action"}], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Descent", "text": ""}, {"name": "Cloak-1", "text": ""}, {"name": "Boardable", "text": ""}, {"name": "Civilian Transport", "text": ""}, {"name": "Elite Fighter Escort", "text": ""}, {"name": "Unique", "text": ""}], "famousPrefix": "Only Ship of the Class:", "famous": ["The Affluent"], "lore": ["The Affluence Class Luxury liner was the one of a kind personal liner of the media mogul Jacen Board. No expense was spared when this ship was designed. Featuring the most advanced propulsion systems available on any civilian vessel, the Affluence is able to travel at staggering speeds, often only matched by ships half its size. This proved incredibly useful when the Affluent was able to outrun several Scourge ships and make an emergency foldspace jump to safety during the opening hours of the Scourge invasion.", "Eventually the Affluent managed to make a calculated jump to Platina, staying in system until it was able to make the jump to Aurum. Here it would stay as a home away from home for Board. While the mogul re-started his media empire, he would never live to see what remained of the old one. It was assumed that the Affluent would spend the rest of its days docked above Aurum. That was until possibly the greatest heist seen since in the history of the UCM.", "The day following the start of the reconquest was one with all focus on the largest military undertaking ever made by humanity, all except for a small few thieves, lurking in the void. Months of planning had lead them to this moment, an effort by over two dozen shipnappers across the Aurum system. To celebrate the start of the Reconquest, the Affluence was brought to a minimal operational readiness, just enough to give the UCM fleet a proper send-off. This was what the thieves were waiting for. Rushing into the conveniently open hangar bay with light dropships, they stormed the Ship’s critical areas and brought the foldspace drive online. Before anyone had time to react, the Affluent was burning hard for the outer marker. Six hours later and the ship vanished from UCM space, and hasn’t been seen since."]}, {"name": "DH-Type Penal Transport", "cost": 123, "tonnage": "M", "art": "dh_type_penal_transport.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "6\"", "scan": "4\"", "sig": "6\"", "hull": 12, "es": "4+", "ks": "4+", "bs": "6+", "g": "1", "special": "Marines-1, Unique, Penal Legions"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Deterrence Missiles", "arc": "F/S", "attack": "4", "lock": "3+", "damage": "1", "type": "K", "special": "Close Action"}, {"name": "Anti-Fighter Lasers", "arc": "F/S/R", "attack": "5", "lock": "3+", "damage": "0", "type": "E", "special": "Anti Wing, Close Action"}], "loads": [{"name": "Drop Pods", "launch": "2", "special": "Alt-1"}, {"name": "Boarding Pods", "launch": "2", "special": "Alt-1"}], "rules": [{"name": "Marines-1", "text": "Remove 1 enemy Battalions from this Ship at the beginning of the Battalion Combat step."}, {"name": "Unique", "text": "You may only take one Group of this Ship."}, {"name": "Penal Legions", "text": "When taken as part of your fleet, this Ship starts the game with 2 friendly Battalions on it. When any number of enemy Battalions are removed due to Boarding Actions or Battalion Combat on a Space Station within 6” of this Ship, place a single friendly Battalion on this Ship. This Ship’s Boarding Pods and Drop Pods can only be used while it has friendly Battalions on it and each Boarding Pod or Drop Pod launched causes one friendly Battalion on this Ship to be removed."}], "famousPrefix": "Known ships of the class:", "famous": ["Dreadhold", "No Mercy", "Last Chance (UCM)", "Infestation (Scourge)", "Blood Money", "Tooth and Claw (Independents)", "DH2745 (Kalium)"], "lore": ["The DH-Type represents one of the Colonial Fleet's largest run of dedicated long-range prison ships, built around a standardized architecture of reinforced armour, multi-tier detention decks and automated security. Originally intended strictly for high-risk inmate transport and remote incarceration, wartime pressures pushed the class into broader operational roles.", "Though designed with consistent core systems, such as compartmentalized containment blocks, automated defensive suites, ECM shielding, and a C.A.G.E emitter field. The ships grew increasingly variable due to differing missions, retrofits, and partial deactivations. Although uncommon, Individual DH-Type vessels gained their own notoriety, such as Iron Veil, Remnant Forge, Dreadhold and Bright Spire. The DH-Type ships illustrated the evolution through conversions into troop transports, logistics carriers, medical ships, and frontier support platforms, often retaining traces of their original penal infrastructure.", "In modern service, L1-class hulls endure as adaptable, if austere, multi-role assets. Their durable construction, intimidating infrastructure, and legacy security systems continue to define their operational character, reflecting both the robustness of the original design and the fleet's ongoing need to repurpose coercive architecture for broader demands."]}, {"name": "Jah’tar Startrader", "cost": 113, "tonnage": "M", "art": "jahetar_startrader.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "12\"", "scan": "6\"", "sig": "8\"", "hull": 10, "es": "5+", "ks": "5+", "bs": "6+", "g": "1", "special": "Aegis-4, Rare, Purchased Power"}, "weapons": [], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Aegis-4", "text": "All Ships with this rule in a Group combine their 4 values into a single value, Y.\nFriendly Groups in coherency within 6” of a Ship with this rule and the same Orbital Layer (including its own Group) gain the benefits of Aegis.\nWhen rolling saves against Close Action and Bomber (of any type) attacks, those Groups gain Y additional save dice they may add to those saves. Before rolling to save, the defending player assigns these dice against specific weapons, divided up as they choose (including any modified hits).\nAn Aegis Group can only grant the benefits of Aegis once each time a friendly group is attacked.\nA friendly Group can only benefit from Aegis from one Group each time it is attacked."}, {"name": "Rare", "text": "You may only take one Group of this Ship in a Skirmish-sized game, two in a Clash, three in a Battle, and four in a Reconquest."}, {"name": "Purchased Power", "text": "This Ship starts the game with 5 wares tokens.\nAt the start of each round, if you control this Ship, you may spend a number of wares tokens on one of the following effects until the end of the round:\nDefence Harmonics - 2 Tokens: Friendly Groups within 6” improve their Energy and Kinetic saves by 1, to a maximum of a 3+.\nEnergy Dissipators - 1 Tokens: Friendly Groups within 9” count as having 2 fewer Spikes.\nGuardian Schoal - 1 Token: Friendly Assets within 9” cannot be the target of enemy weapons with the Anti Wing special rule"}], "famousPrefix": "Known ships of the class:", "famous": ["Bird-in-hand", "Lustrous Glint", "Penny for your Thoughts"], "lore": ["The Jah'tar are an independent, if diminished, starfaring race that sails from the planet Jaheria. Over two century's peaceable trade with the UCM's colony of Platina, they have shared some of their history.", "Their Time of Many Worlds ended roughly three millennia ago when the Great Adversary came. The Jah'tar do not know if any of their other planets survived. Their lifespans of roughly 35 years make this race-memory dimmer than one might expect, but parallels to mankind's own experience was clear, the Scourge were the likely culprits. Surviving artworks show cruder invading ships, but some Jah'tar technology bears limited similarity to Scourge, and most scientists believe it was absorbed and evolved by the enemy. Jah'tar ships also appear grown rather than made, although theirs are largely pseudo-organic chitin over a fine titanium weave.", "The Jah'tar no longer fully understand their own technology. Possibly such knowledge was confined to their lost central worlds, but as in antiquity, all Jah'tar works radiate a passion for style and beauty. They covet precious materials and gems, driving their trade with Platina. In return, the UCM gains access to the Jaherian System's ores and wealth of rare elements essential for FTL drive core construction.", "The Jah'tar are rangier than humans with stronger limbs and thick, leathery skin. Naturally placid and artistic, they move in an unhurried way but are fast when pressed. With long, prehensile tails they are agile climbers, leading to some exotic spaces aboard their ships. Their four, quad-jointed digits are equally dextrous on hands or feet, and are in constant motion, possibly as a base layer of communication. Their language is a series of rapid clicks and screeches, so they use human speech in negotiations out of respect for our limited vocal range.", "Most of humanity's contact with the Jah'tar is via their famous Startraders, graceful, cruiser-sized ships with lavishly decorated meeting spaces, living areas, and cavernous holds. These vessels are permitted free passage within the Platina System but are closely monitored whenever they appear elsewhere in UCM space, despite being unarmed. Hawkish colonial admirals insist that all that internal space could be put to more nefarious uses. Some Startraders serve as mercenaries with other races in exchange for favourable trades, although the UCM occasionally utilises their services so too. Their value lies with their unique support technologies since the Jah'tar refuse to license any true warships to other's violence.", "Relations with the alien Jah'tar is an aberration for the UCM, but these arrangements go back before the Scourge invasion and are frankly easier than conquest. Although Jaheria would inevitably be crushed, Jah'tar weaponry is formidable when they are forced to use it, and high casualties that humanity can ill-afford would result."]}, {"name": "M-Type Barge", "cost": 95, "tonnage": "M", "art": "m_type_barge.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "9\"", "scan": "6\"", "sig": "4\"", "hull": 6, "es": "4+", "ks": "5+", "bs": "6+", "g": "1", "special": "Monitor"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Deterrence Missiles", "arc": "F/S", "attack": "4", "lock": "3+", "damage": "1", "type": "K", "special": "Close Action"}], "loads": [{"name": "Military Outpost", "launch": "1", "special": "Limited-1"}], "rules": [{"name": "Monitor", "text": "Ships with this rule may not use Course Change or Max Thrust orders."}, {"name": "Feature Carrier (Outpost)", "text": "This Ship starts the game carrying a Military Outpost as a Deployable Feature."}, {"name": "Mercenary", "text": "This Ship may be used in any Fleet regardless of faction. When taken as part of your fleet, this Ship loses its Boardable and Civilian Transport rules."}], "famousPrefix": "Known ships of the class:", "famous": ["Ever Astra", "Maersk Olympus", "Foldship Ace", "TTF Shippy"], "lore": ["M-Type Barges are the larger cousin of the L-Type. Produced at the same Tharsis Manufacturing shipyards over Mars, the M-Type was designed for corporate bulk shipping. Many and more of these were owned and operated by the enduring shipping companies of old Earth, each of them emblazoned with corporate livery. Designed and built after the L-Type, these ships feature much improved Foldspace drives as well as the latest innovations in structural bracing. Optimisations in production brought the build time on these freight behemoths down to only twice that of the L-Type.", "Many of these were spared the events of the Scourge invasion, most would have been slowly moving between the colonies and the cradle worlds, far enough away to make emergency jumps to safety. The initial trade and logistics network of the UCM was built upon the backs of the M-Type, their reliability and availability gave the colonies enough trade stability to recover from the loss of the cradle worlds. M-Types are surprisingly rare in Resistance fleets, most of the captains of these ships were more interested in meeting deadlines and quotas than in doomsday predictions prior to the battle of Vega. Kalium is yet to be seen operating these ships, preferring the L-Type for combat resupply, though may potentially be using M-Types in more secure Kalium controlled systems.", "Recent developments in prefabricated defensive structures have allowed a small number of these ships to carry deployable missile defence outposts in place of their normal cargo compliment. These outposts are designed to grant a foothold on a planet and supplement its missile halo while more permanent structures are built, re-purposed, or captured."]}, {"name": "Princess Liner", "cost": null, "tonnage": "M", "art": "princess_liner.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "10”", "scan": "4”", "sig": "3”", "hull": 12, "es": "4+", "ks": "5+", "bs": "-", "g": "1", "special": "Descent, Cloak-1, Boardable, Civilian Transport"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Asteroid Clearance Laser", "arc": "F/S/R", "attack": "2", "lock": "4+", "damage": "1", "type": "E", "special": "Close Action"}], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Descent", "text": ""}, {"name": "Cloak-1", "text": ""}, {"name": "Boardable", "text": ""}, {"name": "Civilian Transport", "text": ""}], "famousPrefix": "Known ships of the class:", "famous": ["Gin and Jump", "Queen Belle", "There and Back Again", "Paperlad (logistics retro-fit)", "Going Nowhere (prison retro-fit)", "Laps of Luxury (VIP transportation retro-fit)"], "lore": ["The Princess Class cruise liner was once a common site in the space around the Cradle World and close to the more picturesque spatial anomalies available to humanity at the time. They were the hallmark of class and distinction among many at the time, and while most were used by the pleasure seeking masses, some were personal transports for those able to afford such luxury and even as covers for covert diplomatic and espionage missions.", "As with so many things, this ended quickly with the Scourge invasion. Ill-equipped to face up to even the lowliest Scourge frigate, Princess Class liners breaking orbit made for tempting and easy targets for the aliens. Most of those seconded to the evacuation effort were easy prey for the Scourge; packed to the seams with refugees, they were a cornucopia of pre-packaged hosts for the insidious race.", "Those few liners that did escape only managed to do so due to their relatively low power output and small signature for a ship of their size – lacking high powered weapons, shields or point defences, they create very little return ping on most sensors.", "Today there is little call for sight-seeing pleasure cruises while the fate of the galaxy hangs in the balance. The vast majority of Princess Class cruise liners still in service are have been retro-fitted for VIP transportation, as mobile prison hulks, or interplanetary logistics vehicles. There are many more still hanging in the void – deserted, dormant, or endlessly orbiting the cradle worlds; the breath taking views they offer seen by none but the dead."]}, {"name": "OBV-64 Oblivion Barge", "cost": 125, "tonnage": "M", "art": "obv_64_oblivion_barge.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "6\"", "scan": "6\"", "sig": "8\"", "hull": 13, "es": "4+", "ks": "5+", "bs": "6+", "g": "1", "special": "Rare, Reinforced Armour"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Expel Hazards", "arc": "F", "attack": "2", "lock": "3+", "damage": "1", "type": "C", "special": "Anti Wing"}], "loads": [{"name": "Mines", "launch": "3", "special": "-"}], "rules": [{"name": "Rare", "text": "You may only take one Group of this Ship in a Skirmish-sized game, two in a Clash, three in a Battle, and four in a Reconquest."}, {"name": "Reinforced Armour", "text": "Weapons rolling to hit this Ship or its Group can only score criticals against it on a result of a 3 higher than its Lock value."}, {"name": "Expel Hazards", "text": "This weapon can only be used against targets within Scan range and on the same Orbital Layer.\nWhile this Ship is below its starting Hull Points, for every 2 Hull Points lost from its starting Hull Points, increase the attack of this weapon by 1."}, {"name": "Acquired Mines", "text": "This Ship's Mines use the stats of its parent fleet."}, {"name": "Mercenary", "text": "This Ship may be used in any fleet regardless of faction. When taken as part of your fleet, this Ship loses its Boardable and Civilian Transport rules."}], "famousPrefix": "Known ships of the class:", "famous": ["Rad Wretch", "Trash Bash", "S-Stain (Independents)", "Volatile Contents Hauler KHC-04a (Kalium)"], "lore": ["The Oblivion OBV64 Barge is a heavily armoured civilian vessel designed to transport extremely hazardous materials, unstable technology, failed reactors, and biohazards, too dangerous to store on planets. These ships travel discreetly between remote depots, derelict battlefields, and disposal zones. Crewed by an extensive team of highly trained specialists under strict quarantine and secrecy protocols, The Oblivion barge handles cargo that is often poorly understood or classified. Their role is to quietly remove dangerous discoveries and remnants from circulation before they can threaten the wider fleet, or attract unwanted attention."]}, {"name": "Argonaut", "cost": 112, "tonnage": "M", "art": "argonaut.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "10\"", "scan": "4\"", "sig": "2\"", "hull": 11, "es": "5+", "ks": "5+", "bs": "6+", "g": "1-2", "special": "Impetuous, Rare"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Thermal Lash", "arc": "F/S/R", "attack": "3", "lock": "3+", "damage": "2", "type": "E", "special": "Scald-2, Sustained Fire"}, {"name": "Force Wave", "arc": "F/S", "attack": "4", "lock": "3+", "damage": "1", "type": "K", "special": "Arrest-2, Impel-2"}], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Impetuous", "text": "At the start of each round, friendly Groups with this rule improve the Lock of their Weapon Systems by 1 until you activate a friendly Group without this rule."}, {"name": "Rare", "text": "You may only take one Group of this Ship in a Skirmish-sized game, two in a Clash, three in a Battle, and four in a Reconquest."}, {"name": "Thermal Lash", "text": "This weapon can only be used against targets in base contact.\nWhen you inflict damage with this weapon, you may remove a Spike from this Group, if you do, the defending Group gains a Spike."}, {"name": "Mind of its Own", "text": "This Ship can be used in any fleet, regardless of faction but does not count towards point spent on M Tonnage Ships when building your fleet. This Ship cannot have an Admiral assigned to it for any reason.\nInstead of picking an Order for this Group when it activates, it may in any order; turn in any direction, move up to its Thrust, attack with any number of its weapons gaining a Spike for each additional Weapon System assigned after the first. Each option can only be chosen once per activation.\nAt the end of this Group's activation, if it did not gain any Spikes, remove a Spike from it."}], "famousPrefix": "Encountered individual:", "famous": ["Astrofauna HD215152-A"], "lore": ["Though there has been extensive speculation on the viability or even potential existence of any kind of life adapted for the vacuum of space, none have been able to prove any hypothesis one way or another. The complete alien nature of something that could feasibly live without any kind of atmosphere or gravity pushes the limits of human speculation. Though themselves alien, every other race humanity has encountered has had a terrestrial origin. PHR expeditionary fleets have almost by accident stumbled into proof of space-based lifeforms. A solitary, anomalous creature was found in a small orange dwarf system. For an as-yet-unknown reason, this creature was traversing a veritable cosmic backwater with nought but ice and gas giants. Seemingly passive, the creature ignored the survey fleet, at least until it closed in. Initially curious, the creature allowed a single survey vessel close enough to scan, though was likely taking in all it could of the strange mechanical interloper.", "It's temperament suddenly changed, however, when a second survey vessel moved to its opposite flank. Without warning, it unleashed a tentacle that damn near tore the closest ship in half. If it wasn't for the quick thinking of the crew the ship could well have been lost to the attack. The flanking ship was hit by an attack with no discernible origin. Crushing forces impacted the ship and though little structural damage was caused, they were pushed into a completely different heading and at a much reduced velocity.", "Fortunately both ships had completed detailed scans of the creature, and although these are currently highly classified, news of this incredible discovery, now dubbed \"The Argonaut\", is reaching the ears of those back in the republic. Unfortunately, both survey ships have been prevented from returning to PHR space and have been instructed to seek the nearest safe-haven to repair and shelter. While the Solar system is hardly safe, it is the largest concentration of PHR assets within a reasonable distance, and is about as safe as anywhere else."]}, {"name": "Type-87 Terminus Harvester", "cost": 210, "tonnage": "H", "art": "type_87_terminus_harvester.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "6\"", "scan": "6\"", "sig": "6\"", "hull": 18, "es": "4+", "ks": "3+", "bs": "5+", "g": "1", "special": "Porter F-2, Reinforced Armour, Monitor"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Colossal Salvage Cutter", "arc": "F", "attack": "5", "lock": "2+", "damage": "3", "type": "C", "special": "Close Action, Bloom-3"}], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Porter F-2", "text": "This Ship may be assigned Payload Ships with the same letter up to a total capacity of 2.\nDuring a Porter’s activation, it may attach any detached Payload Ships within 3” if it has available capacity. Payload Ships reattached to a Porter Ship are removed from the table to be deployed in a later round.\nAny tokens, Spikes, or effects affecting the reattached Payload Ship are removed from that Ship."}, {"name": "Reinforced Armour", "text": "Weapons rolling to hit this Ship or its Group can only score criticals against it on a result of a 3 higher than its Lock value."}, {"name": "Monitor", "text": "Ships with this rule may not use Course Change or Max Thrust orders."}, {"name": "Colossal Salvage Cutter", "text": "This weapon can only be used against targets in base contact."}, {"name": "Scrap Hauler", "text": "If this Group ends its activation within 1\" of a Debris Field, this Group gains a scrap token and cannot gain scrap tokens from that Debris Field for the rest of the game. A Group can have a maximum of 8 scrap tokens at any one time. Any attached Payload ships that have any scrap tokens do not count towards this limit. Whenever another Ship within 6\" of a friendly Ship with this rule is destroyed, pick one of those friendly Ships, that Ship gains a scrap token."}, {"name": "Scratch Bodge Job", "text": "At the end of this Ship's activation, you may remove any number of scrap tokens and choose one of the following:\nScrappy Plating: One friendly Ship within 6\" recovers lost Hull points equal to the amount of scrap tokens removed.\nBodge Repairs: Remove a crippling effect from a friendly Ship within 6\" for each scrap token removed."}, {"name": "Industrial Design", "text": "Improve this Group’s Backup save by 2 when rolling to save hits due to Debris Fields."}, {"name": "Mercenary", "text": "This Ship may be used in any Fleet regardless of faction. When taken as part of your fleet, this Ship loses its Boardable rule."}], "famousPrefix": "Noted ships of the class:", "famous": ["Terminus", "Slag Pit", "Scrap Hammer"], "lore": ["The Type-87 Terminus Harvester is a colossal reclamation vessel built to consume the unrepairable wreckage of war. Its monolithic maw engulfs chunks up to frigate tonnage, feeding them into vast crushing chambers where superheated hydraulic presses obliterate hull plating to slag. Two VX-22 Flensers detach from its hull, peeling derelicts apart and hauling scraps to their final destruction. Ancient, slow-moving, and relentless, it labours, stripping vessels down to raw material. Within its corroded halls, life is harsh. Dim corridors reek of burning metal as air filters struggle against decades of industrial smog.", "The Type-87's wedge-like prow is battered and scarred, worn from decades of grinding through wreckage. Deep gouges and warped plating mark where debris crumpled beneath its relentless push, clearing the way for the behemoth behind.", "A monolithic opening capable of engulfing entire frigates, feeding them into a crushing chamber spanning the volume of a megastructure. Inside, reinforced walls lined with titanic hydraulic presses grind vessels down in a superheated maelstrom of pulverized metal, reducing all to molten slag.", "Equipped with two VX-22 Flensers, these small salvage vessels dock onto the Harvester's hull when idle but detach to roam wreckage fields. They Brutally peel derelicts apart piecemeal while hauling fragmented components to the crushing maw. Though technically separate, they operate as an extension of the Harvester, ensuring no usable scrap escapes consumption."]}, {"name": "VX-22 Flenser", "cost": 50, "tonnage": "L", "art": "vx_22_flenser.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "6\"", "scan": "4\"", "sig": "3\"", "hull": 4, "es": "5+", "ks": "4+", "bs": "6+", "g": "-", "special": "Payload F-1, Vectored"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Sawblade Prow", "arc": "F", "attack": "2", "lock": "2+", "damage": "2", "type": "C", "special": "Close Action, Bloom-1"}], "loads": [], "rules": [{"name": "Payload F-1", "text": "When building your fleet, you may choose as many Payload Ships as you like— tonnage limits do not apply to these Ships, and they have no Group size. All Payload S/L Ships must be assigned to a Porter S/L Ship with the same letter. Payload Ships may not activate or be targeted until detached.\nPayload Ships take up 1 of a Porter Ship’s capacity.\nDuring the Porter Ship’s activation, if it is on an Order that allows it to Launch, you may detach one or more of its Payload Ships and place them within 3” of it. In the round they are detached, these Payloads activate together immediately as part of the Porter Ship’s activation after it has completed its Order. In subsequent rounds, all your Payload Ships count as being part of a single Group. Crippling Effects, Spikes, and other rules that affect an entire Group only affect the targeted Payload Ship.\nPayload Ships always follow General Quarters Orders, even if its Porter is on different Orders. Payload Ships ignore Coherency rules (and do not gain Formation Benefits), have no Lead Ship, are targeted by attacks individually, and these attacks can only damage the targeted Payload Ship.\nIf a Payload Ship is attached to a Porter Ship when that Ship is destroyed, the Payload Ship is destroyed."}, {"name": "Vectored", "text": "This Ship may make an additional turn at any point during its movement, regardless of the Order its Group has taken."}, {"name": "Industrial Design", "text": "Improve this Group’s Backup save by 2 when rolling to save hits due to Debris Fields."}, {"name": "Scrap Collection", "text": "If this Ship ends its activation within 1\" of a Debris Field, this Ship gains a scrap token and cannot gain scrap tokens from that Debris Field for the rest of the game. A Ship with this rule can have a maximum of 3 scrap tokens at any one time. Whenever another Ship within 6\" of a friendly Ship with this rule is destroyed, pick one of those friendly Ships, that Ship gains a scrap token."}, {"name": "Unload", "text": "When you attach this Ship to a Porter Ship, you may have the Porter Ship gain all of this Ship's scrap tokens."}, {"name": "Mercenary", "text": "This Ship may be used in any Fleet regardless of faction. When taken as part of your fleet, this Ship loses its Boardable rule."}], "famousPrefix": "Noted ships of the class:", "famous": ["Wreck & Ruin", "Twisted Metal", "Steel Beams", "Grindcore"], "lore": ["The VX-22 Flensers are compact salvage vessels designed for brutal ship dismantling. Their prow mounted sawblades don't cut cleanly, they tear, shred, and rip through wreckage with unrestrained violence. Designed for aggressive reclamation, they are the smaller, more aggressive sibling to the T-Type Tugboat. Where the Tugboat manoeuvres and stabilizes wreckage for controlled processing, the Flensers gut derelicts with reckless brutality, prioritizing destruction over precision.", "Heavy rotating saws brutally cut through hull plating, breaking it into manageable pieces and scattering debris as they progress. Instead of delicate incision, the Flensers' sawblades operate at maximum torque, chewing through reinforced bulkheads with enough force to buckle surrounding structure.", "Their cutting mechanisms frequently overheat, causing violent energy surges that make their hulls shudder mid operation.", "The Flenser hurls debris into the Type-87 Terminus Harvester's compactor bay, sometimes suffering brutal kickback as the churning machinery spits chunks back out. When it happens, the debris slams into its failing frame, worsening the damage and making every load a gamble.", "Positioned below the cockpit, this reinforced plating shields pilots from wreckage kicked up during cutting operations. Sloped for maximum deflection, it redirects debris that could slam into the hull with deadly force, absorbing impacts before they buckle metal or breach compartments."]}, {"name": "PRK-91 Provenance Ark", "cost": 410, "tonnage": "C", "art": "prk_91_provenance_ark.webp", "stats": {"thrust": "5\"", "scan": "10\"", "sig": "16\"", "hull": 23, "es": "4+", "ks": "4+", "bs": "5+", "g": "1", "special": "-"}, "weapons": [{"name": "Heavy Dual Vent Cannon Turret", "arc": "F/S", "attack": "4", "lock": "3+", "damage": "2", "type": "E", "special": "Fusillade-1, Overcharge, Reave-1"}, {"name": "NC-16 Missile Bank", "arc": "F/S/R", "attack": "6", "lock": "3+", "damage": "1", "type": "K", "special": "Close Action, Volley-2"}, {"name": "Genesis Spikes", "arc": "F/S/R", "attack": "3", "lock": "5+", "damage": "2", "type": "K", "special": "Bombardment, Penetrator"}], "loads": [{"name": "Fighters & Bombers", "launch": "4", "special": "-"}, {"name": "Bulk Landers", "launch": "2", "special": "-"}], "rules": [{"name": "Genesis Spikes", "text": "When this weapon successfully inflicts any amount of damage against a City, place a Mutant Fauna token on that Dropsite. Mutant Fauna tokens are not Battalions and cannot control or contest a Dropsite. When any player deploys any number of Battalions to that Dropsite, if that Dropsite has any Mutant Fauna tokens, those Battalions are only placed on a roll of a 5+. If any Battalions are not placed this way, remove a Mutant Fauna token from that Dropsite. If a Dropsite starts a round with a Mutant Fauna token, remove that token at the end of the round."}, {"name": "Expansive Radiator Systems", "text": "At the start of this Ship's activation, remove two Spikes from it."}, {"name": "Mercenary", "text": "This Ship may be used in any Fleet regardless of faction. When taken as part of your fleet, this Ship loses its Boardable and Civilian Transport rules. This ship's Fighters & Bombers use the stats of its parent fleet (if you included this ship in a Scourge fleet, its Fighters & Bombers would follow the Scourge Fighters & Bombers rules)."}], "famousPrefix": "Known ships of the class:", "famous": ["Provenance", "Endurance (Independents)", "Capitana (Kalium)"], "lore": ["A monolithic vessel of unimaginable scale, the Provenance Ark dwarfs most ships. A precursor to the modular construction found on Coloniser class vessels, these ships were a talisman of hope and expansionism. These are the first major terraforming vessels built by mankind, reaching out into an unknown universe. Built to prepare entire worlds for habitation, it carries vast stores of genetic material, atmospheric stabilizers, and autonomous resource systems. The Ark monitors planetary progress through an extensive network of sensors and automated regulators, adjusting atmospheric composition, maintaining microbial balance, and even modulating gravitational and magnetic fields to stabilize emerging terrains.", "Entire cities once mere schematics, rise, with power grids, transport arteries, and habitation modules ready long before the first settlers arrive. Inside, Construction drones and biotic cultivators orchestrate the birth of forests, oceans, and breathable atmospheres with the precision of a master artisan.", "Many ships of this class feature underslung terraforming torpedo launchers. While near useless in ship to ship combat, these torpedoes are geared towards atmospheric re-entry and contain a plethora of mutagens and nerve agents, some of which would be used on Senator class battlecruisers. Under normal circumstances the use of these would constitute a war crime. Here they are simply used to rid prospective landing areas of their megafauna, causing mass hysteria and aggression in local fauna. Any issues with unruly creatures take care of themselves, and those left over can be cut down by specialised anti-fauna vehicles. Once the LZ is cleared of hostiles, the terraformer can then deploy more traditional terraforming methods."]}],rules:{"Civilian Transport": ["This Ship can only choose the General Quarters order.", "This Ship cannot be attacked unless it is controlled by a player. Players cannot attack a friendly Civilian Transport.", "This Ship cannot be the target of Abilities."], "Boardable": ["This Ship can have Battalions Assigned to it as if it were a Space Station.", "At the start of the round, this Ship is controlled by a Player if only they have any Battalions on it, lasting until the end of the round.", "Players that control a Boardable Ship may activate it as if it were a Ship in their Fleet, after all other Groups have activated."], "Blooming": ["Other friendly Ships within 6” of this Ship are Hidden within its Bloom. Enemy Ships attacking these Hidden Ships ignore 2 of their Group’s Spikes when measuring weapons range.", "This special rule ceases to function while this Ship is not controlled."], "Elite Fighter Escort": ["At the start of each round, this Ship gains 3 Elite Fighter Tokens. Before rolling Kinetic or Energy saves against Close Action and Bomber (of any type) attacks for this ship, you may declare the use of any number of Elite Fighter Tokens.", "Each token used causes this Ship to automatically succeed your choice of 2 of those Energy or Kinetic saves without rolling those dice."]}};
